ficials say 15 residents were  involved two health care aides have been  put on paid leave as police conduct a  criminal investigation  the federal liberals are under fire over  missing mental health spending a marquee  promise in the party's 2021 election  platform four and a half billion dollars  was pledged over five years to help  provinces improve access to mental  health treatment but almost a year since  trudeau said it was a priority none of  the money has materialized jamie morocco  has more  five years ago leanne minicello's mental  health deteriorated to the point where  she worried she would lose custody of  her daughter i was feeling terrible i  mean i had suicidal thoughts and  everything the now 45 year old was  diagnosed with adhd and borderline  personality disorder without  provincially funded therapy she's not  sure she would be here i'm not the norm  i think about the children i think about  the parents and  people who aren't able to get this help  according to the canadian mental health  association the system is overwhelmed  and wait lists are long we knew going  into 2020 that the mental health system  wasn't equipped to deal with the strain  that was was on it prior to the pandemic  and now has only become much worse  mental health should be a priority  in august of last year justin trudeau  promised four and a half billion dollars  to provinces and territories for the new  mental health transfer but no money  including the initial 875 million  supposed to have been spent or budgeted  by now has materialized last week the  federal mental health and addictions  minister faced tough questions about the  promise  the platform promised that money to have  been spent right now so  that was a mistake there were concerns  that the five billion dollars in the  bilateral agreements wasn't transparent  and accountable for the money that was  being spent in march ottawa announced 45  million dollars to develop national  standards to ensure that accountability  in an email to global news bennett said  they will formalize what canadians can  expect in terms of timeliness and  quality of mental health services but  advocates say that's just a delay tactic  accommodations for people dianne young  lost her son to addiction and mental  illness in 2013. nine years later she  runs a not-for-profit treatment center  in his name  funding she says held her back for years  it's frustrating yes  it's sad more than frustrating that the  cost could continue to put canadians  lives at risk jamie morocco global news  toronto  back in the u.s covet 19 vaccinations  have finally started for many of its  youngest americans the rollout begins  after pfizer and modernist shots  covering those aged between six months  and five years got federal approval late  last week allowing roughly 18 million  kids to get protected from the virus  though relatively rare for the age group  about 480 children below five have died  of covet 19 in the u.s  honoring heritage and culture next the  celebrations across canada on this  national indigenous peoples day  national indigenous peoples day was  front and center on google canada's main  page today with a doodle celebrating an  influential first nations artist in  addition to a thunderbird and  anishinaabe florals the illustration  features the portrait of the late norval  morriso also known as copper thunderbird  called the picasso of the north he was  known for depicting traditional stories  spiritual themes and political messages  in his work he also founded the woodland  style that became popular among the  indigenous art community the doodle  itself was designed by first nations  couple blake anjokonib and danielle  morrison  from coast to coast on first nation  metis and inuit territory people  gathered for traditional ceremonies to  mark the occasion and while canada still  has a long way to go on the path towards  truth and reconciliation indigenous  communities proudly share their culture  on this day of remembrance and  celebration heather urex west reports  from treaty 6 territory in edmonton  to the ancestral and unseated lands of  the migma people in halifax  there were sounds of drumming and  dancing as members of many first nations  inuit and metis communities celebrated  the country's 26th national indigenous  peoples day  it's  wonderful to be able to show  you know all aspects of our cultures  here on turtle island  in toronto the day began with a sunrise  ceremony at nathan phillips square where  people gathered around a sacred fire to  make offerings we embrace our  relationships and you know that  beautiful road of reconciliation that  we're walking today we honor  all of the missing and murdered  indigenous women  we also honor all the children who've  been lost  in calgary the traditional territory of  the blackfoot satina iskia nakota and  metis the reconciliation walk to fort  calgary was filled with hope with  national indigenous people's day it's a  celebration of  the goodness too that has gone on  through the generations not just not  just the difficulties i've been feeling  really positively in recent years  i'm seeing more people like me on in the  media you know i'm feeling seen and  represented so  that's been really amazing  the discovery of unmarked graves near  the sites of former residential schools  across the country has prompted a  national reckoning over canada's  treatment of indigenous people and while  there is still a deep and collective  trauma among indigenous communities  there is also cause for great pride we  have a very strong cultural and a robust  community and we contribute  a lot indigenous people are  one and a half times more likely than  mainstream society to be business owners  and successful business owners  one of the many reasons to celebrate the  strength and resiliency of the people  that first called this land home  heather urex west global news calgary  and that is global national for this  tuesday night i'm nitu garcia whether  it's bc quebec or beyond we'll leave you  tonight with more scenes from across the  country today marking this 26 national  indigenous people's day thanks for  watching i'll see you here again  tomorrow have a great night  [Music]  you
 

